Walking a directory skips files with unsupported extensions (`.txt`, `.scss`, `.png`) without any error, listing only `a.md` and exiting 0.
== args
input
== file input/a.md
---
description: Source a.
---
# a
== file input/data.txt
{"a": 1}
== file input/styles.scss
body {}
== file input/logo.png
not really a png
== stdout
glob view: input
input/a.md (4 lines): description: "Source a."
== stderr
== exit 0
